<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baili Xi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baili Xi was a minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> under Duke Mu in the seventh century BCE. Originally an official of the small state of Yu, he was taken captive when Jin conquered it; tradition says Duke Mu ransomed him for five ram skins. As minister he helped make <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> a major power in the west, and he became a model of the able man discovered in obscurity.</p></div>
